" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo create a schematic of the Cartesian product, we create a table and list the elements of the first set $A$ in a row across the top and the elements of the second set $B$ in a column down the left side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/8fe661f4daa7a5bb75dea993f46bbf8970400a798e23da4018d3e4a0b891273d.png)\n\nThen, at each intersection, we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B.$\n\nOur completed $A\\times B$ schematic is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/49270545404b21e8068b35cdb59c756e1f3bc3c22608359c8d7e83389e38c7a4.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "4353cd80f75d0977eb667ddec9022bb1b062516f5ecfd4a15235ed3a42c7f256" "basis" 1434 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657" "basis" 1434 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-wor