y/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/5e14edf4c5890bc213d9a488b9135e142a369ea6ee0259cc183a523b7c5316e4.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "4353cd80f75d0977eb667ddec9022bb1b062516f5ecfd4a15235ed3a42c7f256" "basis" 1434 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-1261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the sets $X={x,y,z},$ $Y={v,w},$ and $Z=X\\times Y,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(x,v)\\in Z$\n- $(y,w)\\in Z$\n- $(w,z)\\in Z$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "4353cd80f75d0977eb667ddec9022bb1b062516f5ecfd4a15235ed3a42c7f256" "basis" 1434 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-1261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian product $X\\times Y$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Y.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $X\\times Y$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/316a12102e4be81291f06403815cfb63749b1fd3f463c465294e031543123484.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(x,v),(x,w),(y,v),(y,w),(z,v),(z,w)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "4353cd80f75d0977eb667ddec9022bb1b062516f5ecfd4a15235ed3a42c7f256" "basis" 1434 "